    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d775">

                <pb facs="1248" n="1234" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1234"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/7–644</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The First Secretary of the British Embassy</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gore-Booth</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Legal Adviser</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hackworth</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Ref: 152/66/44</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-06">6 July, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Hackworth</hi>: I enclose herewith a
                    paraphrase of a telegram we have just received from London about a further
                    possible declaration on the subject of the punishment of war criminals, which is
                    being advocated by the French Committee of National Liberation.</p>
                <pb facs="1249" n="1235" xml:id="pg1235"/>
                <p>As you will see, His Majesty’s Government in the United Kingdom are not in favour
                    of making a further statement on this matter at the present time, and in any
                    case do not think the United Nations War Crimes Commission would be the proper
                    channel for such a declaration.</p>
                <p>I should be grateful if you would let me know whether you agree with the Foreign
                    Office views, and if so whether I may tell them that you will be replying on
                    similar lines to the French Committee.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>P. H. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gore-Booth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d775-a1.xml" xpointer="d775-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
